# Findings a person has looked at and accepted. One line per finding, as
# path:rule:line, or commit:path:rule:line for a finding in history -- a
# fingerprint suppresses exactly that finding and nothing else.
#
# Deliberately NOT a .gitleaks.toml allowlist. An allowlist entry keyed on a
# path excludes that whole file from every rule, even with condition = "AND":
# measured on this repository, two randomly generated secrets planted in the
# allowlisted files went from 4 findings to 0. A fingerprint cannot do that --
# it names one rule at one line, and anything else in the same file is still
# reported.
#
# Re-check after editing this file, the only way that means anything -- plant a
# random secret in one of the files below, confirm it is still caught, remove it.
#
